  (note 16 "ἐπεφέρετο, imperfect middle/passive of ἐπιφέρω: \"was being borne\" (or \"was moving\") over the water. Translations from the Hebrew have \"was hovering\"; the Greek verb does not say \"hover\". The table has no lemma for the form; ἐπιφέρω is supplied. The readable layer says \"was moving\": \"was being borne\" is not natural modern English (owner, 2026-11-26), and \"moving\" keeps the Greek's sense of being carried along without adding \"hovering\".")
  (note 19 "ὕδατος is singular (\"the water\"), as in 1:6-9; the Hebrew is plural (\"the waters\"). The Greek turns plural at 1:10."))

